  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Brig. Thota Ramaiah, vs The State Of Telangana on 15 April, 2024 Author: T. Vinod Kumar Bench: T. Vinod Kumar The Hon'Ble Sri Justice T. Vinod Kumar Writ Petition No.13532 of 2023 Order:",
    "facts": "This Writ Petition is filed for issuance of a Writ of Mandamus to declare the inaction of respondent No.3 in taking action against respondent No.4 despite petitioners' complaint dated 10-04-2023 through respondent No.5 and representation dated 02-05-2023 as illegal, arbitrary, unjust and violative of Article 14 of the Constitution of India. Brig. Thota Ramaiah, vs The State Of Telangana on 15 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/151291930/ 1 7. Petitioners further contend that the 5th respondent, on the basis of the aforesaid representation submitted by them, had addressed letter dated 10-04-2023 to the 3rd respondent and requested the 3rd respondent not to permit any commercial activity and also not to give any permission/license in favour of the 4th respondent.",
    "arguments": "14. The 4th respondent further claims that he had obtained registration certificate number under the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India as issued by the Government of Telangana and also obtained certificate of registration from the Labour Department and as such, the setting of cafeteria/canteen in the subject premises cannot be objected to by the petitioners. 15. The 4th respondent further contended that there are other similar commercial establishments which are in existence in the area and as such, setting up of cafeteria/canteen by him alone cannot Brig. Thota Ramaiah, vs The State Of Telangana on 15 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/151291930/ 2 be held to be an illegal activity."
  },
